      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are right to feel that a happy ending feels dishonest, but the most honest ending for Elias isn’t a happy one—it’s a quiet, quiet resignation that lets him finally stop trying to fix things. He can choose to step out of the way, not as a hero, but as a person who has finally accepted that he is just another part of the world, and that is enough. He can let go of the weight of his own making and simply exist, and in that act of existence, he becomes the peace he was looking for.",
